    {
      "title": "IGL raises CNG price by Rs 3.89 per kg in Delhi as LNG costs surge",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/igl-raises-cng-price-by-rs-3-89-per-kg-in-delhi-as-lng-costs-surge-126082900349_1.html",
      "description": "CNG will cost Rs 86.98 per kg in Delhi from August 29, with IGL citing higher imported spot LNG prices following renewed disruption around the Strait of Hormuz",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-29T08:02:08"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delhi autorickshaw bodies demand hike in fares after CNG price rise",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-autorickshaw-bodies-demand-hike-in-fares-after-cng-price-rise-126082900270_1.html",
      "description": "With CNG prices increased in Delhi, city-based transport bodies on Saturday demanded an immediate hike in autorickshaw fares and threatened to go on a strike on September 9 if their demand was not fulfilled.\nThe price of CNG in Delhi and adjoining cities increased by Rs 3.89 per kg from Saturday, according to Indraprastha Gas Ltd.\nIt said a significant portion of input gas for CNG was being met through imported LNG, whose rates in the spot or current market had seen a surge since the beginning of the West Asia conflict.\nAuto Rickshaw Association and Delhi Pradesh Taxi Union General Secretary Rajendra Soni said, \"The Delhi government should increase auto and taxi fares with immediate effect within one week, as CNG prices were increased by Rs 3.89 this morning, which has suddenly increased the financial burden on poor drivers.\"\nCNG prices have been rising over the past two to three months, with a cumulative increase of approximately Rs 10-11, he said in a statement.\n\"The government",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-29T06:25:04"
    }
